lines += [f"Generic 64-slot pool preparation {deploy['ready']['preparation_ms']:.3f} ms; service startup through all templates and pool ready {deploy['service_start_to_ready_ms']:.3f} ms (binaries already built).",f"Refill work median/max {rs['elapsed_ms']['median']:.3f}/{rs['elapsed_ms']['max']:.3f} ms; retirement-to-replacement including unchanged 1000 ms delay {rs['replacement_ms']['median']:.3f}/{rs['replacement_ms']['max']:.3f} ms.",'', 'Implementation and safety:', 'Preparation closes the existing lifecycle barrier, excludes concurrent trusted ExecVMProcess operations, freezes all non-agent userspace through the freezer cgroup, and checks all visible TCP states including LISTEN. PID1 agent, tracing disabled, compatible freezer hierarchy and same network namespace are required. All unsupported/busy/nonempty cases use the original cleanup path. Source capture release thaws applications. The snapshot preserves the frozen group and token-owned exec lease. The durable manifest only requests the optimization; the guest verifies its own certificate and FROZEN state. Identity/entropy/network updates finish before thaw/publication. Ordinary running-parent fork requests no skip. The freeze-and-record transaction has no async cancellation point; ForkControl requests serialize. No changes to persistence sync barriers or CopyOnWrite restore mode.','', 'Validation:', '20/20 formal fork leases requested and actually used the certified skip (sample-certificates.json). Three templates certified. Guest executable residency was zero for both languages before formal runs. Both products used no language-specific prewarm (preflight artifacts).','Empty certificate blocks trusted execution while frozen; source thaw restores execution; a listener invalidates certificate; a forged skip request without guest certificate falls back to cleanup. Wrong owner and invalid network keep lifecycle barrier closed. Corrupt staged binding is rejected/reclaimed.','Live-parent fork preserves parent TCP connection, resets inherited child connection, and keeps child listener/new connections working. Child process PID/nonce inherits; sampled 303 shared PFNs and independent 16MiB buffer writes verified CoW. Parent-first, child-first and grandchild-after-parent destruction succeed. Node/Ruby interpreters execute in both forks and survivors. Distinct MAC/IP/CID, mutual HTTP, rw-p RAM-file mappings verified.','Seven barrier tests and private-network-namespace TCP test pass. The latter verifies empty namespace, listener rejection, active connection destruction, listener survival and no FD accumulation.','',f"Final owned fork pool: 64 ready, 0 assigned. Service FD count before/after = 2239/{res['totals']['fds']}; PSS {res['totals']['Pss']/1024:.2f} MiB. Isolated mlink list empty and service stopped; original bench108-mlink PID 4034067/start Nov16 18:03:45 unchanged. No other users' processes stopped or modified.",'', 'Harness note: first certificate-only functional harness attempt hit E2B SDK exception on expected `test -f` exit 1; fixed polling to use `|| true`, sandbox cleaned in finally, then functional checks passed. This was before formal measurement and no benchmark sample was rerun.','', 'Artifacts: stages.json, source/, changes.patch, provenance.json, per-sample node/ and ruby/ JSON, validation JSON, preparation/refill records.']
